            <ArticleTitle>The clinical implications of balloon rupture during cardiovascular interventions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E45-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Balloon rupture is an infrequent complication of cardiac catheterization that can lead to vessel injury. We report 6 cases that highlight the potential consequences of balloon rupture, including perforation, dissection, balloon entrapment, and distal embolization, and discuss prevention and treatment strategies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
